.TH MERMAN-CLI-DETECT 1 2026-08-15 "Merman 0.8.0-alpha.6" "Merman CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
merman\-cli\-detect \- Detect the Mermaid diagram type
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmerman\-cli detect\fR [\fB\-\-resource\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-resource\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIINPUT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detect the Mermaid diagram type
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIINPUT\fR]
Input Mermaid file. Use `\-` for stdin
.SH "SOURCE LIMITS"
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR [default: trusted\-native]
Resource policy used to bound source acquisition
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
interactive: General interactive applications and public binding surfaces
.IP \(bu 2
constrained: Constrained rendering for untrusted or publicly submitted documents
.IP \(bu 2
trusted\-native: Local CLI and controlled native batch rendering
.IP \(bu 2
unbounded\-for\-trusted\-input: Explicitly disable policy budgets while retaining hard backend capabilities
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-limit\fR \fI<max_source_bytes=POSITIVE_U64>\fR
Override source bytes as max_source_bytes=POSITIVE_U64
.SH EXTRA
More options: `merman\-cli detect \-\-help` shows source resource controls.
.SH VERSION
v0.8.0\-alpha.6
